oned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/d222e86f6af7c3ed2b35711114c9062d6f0c9b0f2551aa44cac33318c6e5813f.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,x+2\\le y\\le \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\le y\\le x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368898 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368899 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368900 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368901 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368902 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368901 13194139535833 true] [17592186368897 1110 #uuid "2ead9de1-ec2f-5964-af1d-fd2d935607b9" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368898 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368898 1111 #uuid "9e2b1a5b-0afd-51d1-b78f-19d89622ce20" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368899 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368899 1111 #uuid "8c555b30-698b-5508-91ae-8a5b523368fc" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368900 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368900 1111 #uuid "629caba4-f2c8-5694-9b2f-6262758c871b" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368901 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368901 1111 #uuid "b4d0848c-1259-5a5e-a940-79f1fec2ec2c" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368902 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368902 1111 #uuid "1d5e940a-18d6-5803-9bf7-4372db8fb2ff" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368903 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368904 13194139535833 true] [17592186368903 1089 "q-132385" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368903 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535833 true] [17592186368903 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/a4515d2789a9b5c7a08210c0ef2611e7b6e661850b1fa822016b880427088bae.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2},$ and the lines $y=2-x$ and $y=x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368903 1113 #uuid "a88b2724-df79-5926-a981-b520191fb2e9" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368903 1145 "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=-\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=2-x & \\,⟹\\,x=2-y \\\\ y=x & \\,⟹\\,x=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/78aa61f11856dbf35287a0af016b56744fec354d6c4e64690a1a6fe466f164e8.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le y}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,-\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le 2-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368905 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368906 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368907 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368908 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368909 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368906 13194139535833 true] [17592186368904 1110 #uuid "a79ee524-8165-55bb-bd18-8e520d9464e1" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368905 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2-y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368905 1111 #uuid "5a211c1d-44e2-53eb-a40c-2afe07c65a81" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368906 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368906 1111 #uuid "04609af8-1b21-57b5-8205-603182f6b744" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368907 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{-\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368907 1111 #uuid "fccd1a97-5e4a-5a93-969a-98227ab66ae2" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368908 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368908 1111 #uuid "aa87ef4e-5709-5f34-a494-a0d8a14fbb16" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368909 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2-y}^{-\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368909 1111 #uuid "87531304-de0a-54be-9266-2b02f7001467" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368910 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368911 13194139535833 true] [17592186368910 1089 "q-132391" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368910 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368910 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={e}^{x},$ and the lines $y=1-x$ and $x=1.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368910 1113 #uuid "cd98531c-9c3a-58d9-a39c-eb25bb6f031c" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368910 1145 "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={e}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ y=1-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/0c61de3680b68dcf16267483fe1a51f0ef0e4c8247104215ae319d6c01b7a571.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c2a3cd01f74a2adb96e13212916dbb1b4476040d701ccd755258bd22fdefa5de.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1-y\\le x\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\le x\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368912 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368913 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368914 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368915 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368916 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368915 13194139535833 true] [17592186368911 1110 #uuid "51a89ae5-5dfb-5651-9740-fcdca2c0b229" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368912 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368912 1111 #uuid "dc789ae7-6068-54ff-9f22-27223fc51909" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368913 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368913 1111 #uuid "c5e26f71-a2b3-5439-8629-250bfb81046a" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368914 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368914 1111 #uuid "38d29830-ca2f-591a-8bf3-c63c8ac04146" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368915 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368915 1111 #uuid "7e444c51-1c17-5ac2-9d31-afb3f75b2448" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368916 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368916 1111 #uuid "5e14e716-f454-566d-8e11-a60bd9dc04a4" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368917 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368918 13194139535833 true] [17592186368917 1089 "q-132397" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368917 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368917 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-x,$ $y=6-4x$ and $y=2x.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368917 1113 #uuid "cf42f9c9-2acd-54b4-a37d-2acf279d635d" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368917 1145 "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-x & \\,⟹\\,x=-y \\\\ y=6-4x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4} \\\\ y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/08237d1ca2e01d0cf620dfa06a4265d8053b7ee34d0b65036aad7d5734726e1c.png)\n\n \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c756dc7924fc4c116601da907eb3b767b8a40647e063c146dad83b0ea660933b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368919 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368920 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368921 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368922 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368923 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368919 13194139535833 true] [17592186368918 1110 #uuid "60ae2c67-5924-52d5-a137-61bd2cd2965b" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368919 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368919 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368919 1111 #uuid "71db9016-b8a1-538e-a7e2-e2d0c69a67a3" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368920 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368920 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368920 1111 #uuid "bdf0dd73-9a46-568c-9491-2b69fc43e4ae" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368921 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368921 1111 #uuid "705abc50-237c-56ce-8f6a-c617f48bb020" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368922 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{6-4y}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368922 1111 #uuid "1f89cfc2-4bc8-5b6c-8c9e-1f150b64653a" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368923 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368923 1111 #uuid "c975e734-6b56-55ba-8ebe-bc059d4599c9" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368924 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368925 13194139535833 true] [17592186368924 1089 "q-132423" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368924 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368924 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/a4265e8993b5c7ea5756fe55facd5313e5c2237cbdbc851195ebf458e5246060.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368924 1113 #uuid "98fde332-e10f-5706-8291-a4bf10d842e4" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368924 1145 "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/33a38da74b282f0ec1fb2fae9cb155feb2a5fd39128c7607b80c6b84fedd29b4.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 3-x}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,3-x\\le y\\le x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x-1}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{3-x}^{x-1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{x-1}^{3-x}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{3-x}^{x-1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}[(x-1)^{2}-(3-x)^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(8-4x)\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(4x-8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(8x-2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{2}+(2{x}^{2}-8x){|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(2-1)-2({2}^{2}-{1}^{2})+2({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})-8(4-2) \\\\  & =8-6+24-16 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368926 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368927 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368928 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368929 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368930 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368928 13194139535833 true] [17592186368925 1110 #uuid "a2fa8e2e-27dd-53f6-9fa5-caef34f379da" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368926 1034 "12" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368926 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368926 1111 #uuid "d712e608-39fa-53d3-99d0-4c7b613f7c82" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368927 1034 "\\frac{71}{3}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368927 1111 #uuid "59e551d3-cc68-5d06-9e3d-938b3ec6eeab" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368928 1034 "10" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368928 1111 #uuid "098809cb-ae5c-57fb-8d4f-d5971c2a9b39" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368929 1034 "\\frac{55}{3}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368929 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368929 1111 #uuid "c1b588a4-6813-5252-907d-7241cde00cdb" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368930 1034 "\\frac{55}{2}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368930 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368930 1111 #uuid "eaba30a1-03f3-5225-a164-814bae7b3995" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368931 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368932 13194139535833 true] [17592186368931 1089 "q-82074" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368931 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535833 true] [17592186368931 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={e}^{x},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$  and the lines $y=1-x$  and $y=1+e-x.$ \nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368931 1113 #uuid "bb21676e-08c7-5934-b467-875d09f0ef3a" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368931 1145 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/4854afc35aff7cfb47ba09481f975b22e41f3309b08a2ba7c409a4bbd32c8601.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/50c5b7a864099f512515ab2db4c1596382883e93f7d4b23b9d16b91e42e3021b.png)\n\n   \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 1+e-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368933 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368934 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368935 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368936 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368937 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368935 13194139535833 true] [17592186368932 1110 #uuid "ea0d6ca8-8cd2-5a5f-b12a-468115e606ca" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368933 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1+x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e+x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368933 1111 #uuid "c0bbe2af-9d09-51e5-adba-f0b49a28ba82" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368934 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368934 1111 #uuid "b2ce1c0e-6121-5bfc-aafa-62d26a83a333" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368935 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368935 1111 #uuid "65bf628d-dba1-5661-947b-7b5bb930c8f9" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368936 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e+x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368936 1111 #uuid "3ad46bcf-8381-55d3-85fe-2dd85e06a1ac" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368937 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368937 1111 #uuid "3a89703a-7e06-5b6a-9932-35678d8b5a37" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368938 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368939 13194139535833 true] [17592186368938 1089 "q-82137" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368938 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368938 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={2}^{x},$ $y=\\sqrt{x}$  and lines $y=1$ and $y=6-x.$\nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368938 1113 #uuid "5b241a60-d8fd-5bf0-9caf-5547e75ebf63" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368938 1145 "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={2}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={log}_{2}⁡y \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2} \\\\ y=6-x & \\,⟹\\,x=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/fe95bc4ca8c687c79fe1c475eb1d8001d71a41ba34e076ad7fdfa8391cb08839.png)\n\n   \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/099c35cbab4dfdd4a94207ed950fbdca8b8e766a612fb5e665e7d443d75ec050.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,{log}_{2}⁡y\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 4,\\,{log}_{2}⁡y\\le x\\le 6-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368940 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368941 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368942 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368943 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368944 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368941 13194139535833 true] [17592186368939 1110 #uuid "013b6830-3c84-51bc-8e87-b87591928ab9" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368940 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}^{4}{\\int }_{{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368940 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368940 1111 #uuid "ae8a186f-9167-5a80-9dda-2d9e8aa2ba7e" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368941 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368941 1111 #uuid "a3607d52-792c-5ea8-a8c7-224cba16f32d" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368942 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}{\\int }_{2}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}^{4}{\\int }_{{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368942 1111 #uuid "79995432-87ba-5cf3-b7fa-1e0e4a2c82b0" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368943 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368943 1111 #uuid "6addd573-a9b0-5c7f-b48e-735975050ebb" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368944 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368944 1111 #uuid "62d3ac6b-1b58-52b0-ad10-1a111cde2664" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368945 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368946 13194139535833 true] [17592186368945 1089 "q-82223" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368945 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368945 1100 "${∬}_{|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}\\,\\,6(x+y)\\,dA=$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368945 1113 #uuid "436c8a72-dab1-585b-85dc-3a344114e654" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368945 1145 "First, let's draw a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c9072d2b8f1b49770403280af13d3d8e681247f168e796c056eb697fe28b8ba9.png)\n\n  \n\nThe  region $D={(x,y)|\\,\\,|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}$ can be  partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/d16296029378c7adb891affba63683971ff972b5ed0268641ac3b677c694b5f8.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le 2-y}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y\\le x\\le y+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}6(x+y)^{2}\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}6(x+y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}6(x+y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}6(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{y+2}6(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3(x+y)^{2}]_{y}^{2-y}\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[3(x+y)^{2}]_{-y}^{y+2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3(4-4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3(2y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3{[4y-\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1}+4{[(y+1)^{3}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =8+4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368947 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368948 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368949 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368950 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368951 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368947 13194139535833 true] [17592186368946 1110 #uuid "6e0120ab-aa95-51ed-8ee1-dbad7f59f2f1" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368947 1034 "12" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368947 1111 #uuid "420d2f05-4dc3-5b9f-a4f5-d45f9401d57b" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368948 1034 "9" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368948 1111 #uuid "3c3c2501-e46c-5969-a051-950d46653d82" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368949 1034 "3" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368949 1111 #uuid "43a8cbc1-fbc7-5ead-847c-e34b61988a19" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368950 1034 "15" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368950 1111 #uuid "87b0d9e4-62bf-56a0-afc1-7180317b7cfe" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368951 1034 "6" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368951 1111 #uuid "b9271914-7718-5fac-a491-9c3528f0f523" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368952 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368953 13194139535833 true] [17592186368952 1089 "q-82229" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368952 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368952 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/ebb0b09ffab6ffdff6a04104b09d6904302fdb7580262663b5e0c65bd3f95502.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curve $y=(x-1)^{2}$ and the lines $y=x+1$ and $y=3-x,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA.$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368952 1113 #uuid "3dcdfeb1-c7df-5260-bb38-cfc091e51c68" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368952 1145 "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/f26c3e1bbbc268308db8d419bc799ad5349673e97c8828471997a5d36cb94d7d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x+1}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le 3-x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x+1)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1}+{[-\\frac{(3-x)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =((\\frac{8}{3}-0)-(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{5}))+((-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5})-(-\\frac{8}{3}-0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}+\\frac{32}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368954 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368955 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368956 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368957 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368958 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368956 13194139535833 true] [17592186368953 1110 #uuid "b0c9084e-dcce-5597-82b6-de8e535380f9" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368954 1034 "\\frac{78}{5}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368954 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368954 1111 #uuid "96bd6456-1c50-50ec-9299-af511d678379" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368955 1034 "\\frac{48}{5}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368955 1111 #uuid "4717a8f1-7cde-50a9-bc5f-ed423f37adbe" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368956 1034 "\\frac{64}{15}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368956 1111 #uuid "74763c02-2a94-5520-ac2f-fd98170a1c4a" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368957 1034 "\\frac{84}{25}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368957 1111 #uuid "a1d04c91-ee9c-55d1-aca3-aea23efc376d" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368958 1034 "\\frac{106}{25}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368958 1111 #uuid "521ab99a-f7b0-52b3-bf38-cbff26aefe20" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368959 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368960 13194139535833 true] [17592186368959 1089 "q-82355" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368959 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535833 true] [17592186368959 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=-6{x}^{2}+24x-17$ and lines $y=6x-5,$ $x=3,$ and $y=1.$\nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368959 1113 #uuid "13e33bff-8759-571b-aca8-15a30bd49e5a" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368959 1145 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/fe0209b3ed99aae4a1a939dfc7a8e0e400976809cc220abb1fbdf2f766c76171.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c8ba7d6923e2e4ef9ee528c48a8f5664ec10e4f05a13dad941713600d93ddfe5.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 6x-5}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le -6{x}^{2}+24x-17}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368961 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368962 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368963 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368964 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368965 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368963 13194139535833 true] [17592186368960 1110 #uuid "c13c3b64-0d06-5b45-8774-5371a6d897ba" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368961 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368961 1111 #uuid "07f4f08e-c1f1-578a-b36b-a2f91a43caeb" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368962 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368962 1111 #uuid "4c5ffa47-dcbb-5d71-8aa4-25185c7285cb" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368963 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368963 1111 #uuid "4a5629ae-9c80-548d-a66c-815c9e50d338" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368964 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368964 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368964 1111 #uuid "743720b2-5ee9-5e2f-b742-3ef3aa2d0829" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368965 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368965 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368965 1111 #uuid "9cbb48d3-a416-533a-906d-5d61bd9c3c83" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368966 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368967 13194139535833 true] [17592186368966 1089 "q-82360" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368966 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368966 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/ad8d4069ab0effd57ba58ccc4bf5792d5a014b114afb086e6d4b71d69ba14d2c.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=|x|,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2x\\,dA.$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368966 1113 #uuid "4837c157-fc9f-5c75-9787-2e74e7f04e9c" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368966 1145 "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/2fcb30778db2f051a7a819ae701808af59ac18d27c25a9c57ce678caa6c3ee3b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le -x}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2x\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2x\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2x\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2x[-x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2x[x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{-1}^{0}+{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =((0-(-\\frac{2}{3}(-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{4}))+((\\frac{2}{3}(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{4})-0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368968 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368969 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368970 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368971 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368972 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368972 13194139535833 true] [17592186368967 1110 #uuid "0d825b63-fc7e-5f47-8f54-0cdec494c88d" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368968 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368968 1111 #uuid "028be94a-72c2-5f0e-ae1e-ed4916e6b1c5" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368969 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368969 1111 #uuid "f81f41a8-8294-5051-90f1-b8c9edf5901f" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368970 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368970 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368970 1111 #uuid "c0caca54-652d-5656-8be2-c80e091f86f5" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368971 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368971 1111 #uuid "90ae483c-4995-55a9-a506-d6c35df47cf4" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368972 1034 "0" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [17592186368972 1111 #uuid "5825effa-fe41-5333-b60f-701fb3285424" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368973 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368974 13194139535833 true] [17592186368973 1089 "q-82362" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368973 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535833 true] [17592186368973 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/13275042f8b7b74e394b3cee1350c19cfa50ddf63899066682cbd0109f42d6bf.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." 13194139535833 true] [17592186368973 1113 #uuid "964b4bf4-f010-55d7-af2e-96cfe4a3d003" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368973 1145 "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/648121ff2a676f6a472a6e221dffe813eca55f914aed0ca9a285bb0d4cd81ab3.png)\n\n   \n\nAs a result, we get \n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}4xy\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}4xy\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(9-1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}2x(9-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}16x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}18x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}+9{x}^{2}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =8(4-0)+9(9-4) \\\\  & =77.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368975 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368976 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368977 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368978 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368979 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1041 "selection" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368978 13194139535833 true] [17592186368974 1110 #uuid "25abd9bc-6970-541f-ab75-8f0cb65594b0" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368975 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139535833 true] [17592186368975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535833 true] [1759218636897